--TEST--
Explain versions removed by different policies that would avoid a conflict on a transitively required package.
--COMPOSER--
{
    "name": "acme/project",
    "version": "1.0.0",
    "require": {
        "acme/conflicter": "1.0.0",
        "acme/app": "1.0.0"
    },
    "config": {"policy": {"advisories": {"block": true}, "cooldown": {"period": "1 week"}}},
    "repositories": [
        {
            "type": "package",
            "package": [
                {"name": "acme/conflicter", "version": "1.0.0", "conflict": {"acme/lib": ">=1.1"}, "published-time": "2020-01-01T00:00:00+00:00"},
                {"name": "acme/app", "version": "1.0.0", "require": {"acme/lib": "^1.0"}, "published-time": "2020-01-01T00:00:00+00:00"},
                {"name": "acme/lib", "version": "1.0.0", "published-time": "2020-01-01T00:00:00+00:00"},
                {"name": "acme/lib", "version": "1.0.1", "published-time": "2999-01-01T00:00:00+00:00"},
                {"name": "acme/lib", "version": "1.1.0", "published-time": "2020-01-01T00:00:00+00:00"}
            ],
            "security-advisories": {
                "acme/lib": [{
                    "advisoryId": "PKSA-1234-abcd-1234",
                    "packageName": "acme/lib",
                    "remoteId": "test",
                    "title": "Security Advisory",
                    "link": null,
                    "cve": null,
                    "affectedVersions": "<1.0.1",
                    "source": "Tests",
                    "reportedAt": "2024-04-30 12:37:47",
                    "composerRepository": "Package Repository",
                    "severity": "high",
                    "sources": [{"name": "Security Advisory", "remoteId": "test"}]
                }]
            }
        }
    ]
}
--RUN--
update

--EXPECT-EXIT-CODE--
2

--EXPECT-OUTPUT--
Loading composer repositories with package information
<warning>1 package version(s) withheld by the cooldown policy (run with -vv to list them).</warning>
Updating dependencies
Your requirements could not be resolved to an installable set of packages.

  Problem 1
    - Root composer.json requires acme/app 1.0.0 -> satisfiable by acme/app[1.0.0].
    - Root composer.json requires acme/conflicter 1.0.0 -> satisfiable by acme/conflicter[1.0.0].
    - acme/app 1.0.0 requires acme/lib ^1.0 -> satisfiable by acme/lib[1.1.0].
    - acme/conflicter 1.0.0 conflicts with acme/lib 1.1.0.
    - acme/lib[1.0.0, ..., 1.0.1] match the requirements and are not excluded by the conflicts above, but were not loaded, because:
      - 1.0.0: affected by security advisories ("PKSA-1234-abcd-1234")
      - 1.0.1: still in the cooldown period configured in "policy.cooldown" (available in %s)
      Go to https://packagist.org/security-advisories/ to find advisory details. To ignore the advisories, add their IDs to the "policy.advisories.ignore-id" config or add the package to "policy.advisories.ignore". To exempt the package from the cooldown policy, add it to the "policy.cooldown.ignore" config, or run the command with --no-cooldown for a one-off bypass. To turn a policy off entirely, you can set "policy.advisories.block" or "policy.cooldown.block" to false.

--EXPECT--
